WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.150
I'm honored to be able to stand
before all of you, extremely

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.800
humbled to be able
to stand here today.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:27.360
Recently, I wrote to Chief
DiFava and several members

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.460
of the MIT police department.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.540
I wanted them to know that I
had been keeping all police

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:38.450
officers in my
thoughts and prayers.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.750
I told them, as I
will tell you, that I

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:46.489
know that this is a
difficult time for all of us.

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:48.659
And judging by our
numbers here today,

00:00:48.659 --> 00:00:51.670
and by the intensive
conversations

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.120
that we have shared,
I also know that it

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.629
has been extremely hard for us
to continuously witness-- even

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:04.710
from a distance-- the tragic
deaths of innocent men

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.190
and women.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.640
Often, black men and
women, as well as

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.600
the tragic deaths of
police officers committed

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:19.070
to their profession; officers
who were fulfilling their duty

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.080
to protect and serve.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.550
On this latter
point, I would like

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.540
to make a declarative statement.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.920
But in doing so, I
acknowledge that I

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:38.140
am taking a liberty, a liberty
that will enable me to attempt

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.720
to speak for most black people.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.580
And speaking for most, not
to mention all black people,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.070
is not something
that I take lightly.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:54.820
But today, I take this
liberty because I truly

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.070
believe that I
stand with most when

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.800
I say that as black
people specifically,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:08.340
we believe that what
happened in Dallas was wrong.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.680
It was heartbreaking.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:17.090
It was a grave injustice in
the face of so many others.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:21.370
And most of us would not only
agree with Dr. King's words,

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.569
we would espouse them
as our personal beliefs.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:29.410
"Returning violence for
violence multiplies violence,

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:35.230
adding deeper darkness to a
night already devoid of stars.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.030
Darkness cannot drive
out darkness," he says,

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.330
"only light can do that.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:48.670
Hate cannot drive out hate,
only love can do that."

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:53.230
Clearly, feelings of
helplessness, hurt, anger,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.390
and rage have been
expressed here today;

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.080
feelings that many
of us in this room

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.069
have been concealing and
holding in for far too long.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:06.569
These feelings are
genuine, and in many ways,

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:10.450
unavoidable, and
certainly undeniable.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.709
We need and deserve
time to grieve.

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:17.680
Life, however, has
taught me that if we

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.740
stay in a state of
helplessness too long,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.540
it can and will cloud our
vision, our perspective,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.069
and our reality.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:32.459
Because in reality,
we as individuals,

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:37.750
and certainly we as the MIT
community, are not helpless.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.459
For MIT is renowned in
name, many in numbers,

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.130
powerful in presence, and
virtually unparalleled

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:50.120
in our capacity to solve the
world's greatest challenges.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.319
In fact, when it comes to
solving the world's greatest

00:03:54.319 --> 00:04:00.170
problems, the world
often looks to us.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:03.020
In the space called
problem-solving,

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:10.209
MIT sits in a unique and
often unrivaled position.

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:15.569
So my MIT family, I do not
believe that we are helpless,

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:18.069
because only a university
with a president who

00:04:18.069 --> 00:04:22.710
is confident in its ability to
positively impact and influence

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.819
social, political,
and economic change

00:04:25.819 --> 00:04:29.690
would challenge itself,
its students, its faculty,

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:36.470
its staff, and its alumni
to make a better world.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.820
As a nation I do
not believe that we

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.720
are incapable of rising
above our current state.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.020
We can seek peace.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.800
We can implement legislation
policies, practices,

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.910
and a level of democratic
and community policing

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.830
that will not only
heal our land,

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.740
but increase trust and create
an environment that ensures

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.290
safety and security for all.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:08.410
So today, I urge us not
to give into the darkness,

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.010
the darkness of doubt and fear.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.380
Instead, let us
embrace the light

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.850
that shines so
brightly within each

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.990
of our hearts and our minds.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.650
For it has been said that
our deepest fear is not

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.790
that we are inadequate,
our deepest fear

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:29.400
is that we are powerful
beyond measure.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.500
It is our light,
not our darkness,

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.870
that most frightens us.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.160
And that light, my friends,
that life-giving, life-changing,

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.639
infinitely powerful and
brilliantly fueled light

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:52.050
is not just in some of us, it
is in each and every one of us.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:56.410
So we must boldly and
responsibly shine our lights.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:00.229
We must carry our torches,
our lanterns, our beacons,

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:03.400
our light sabers.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.180
We must carry them
as symbols of hope

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.970
and use them for
good, for they will

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.759
be a lamp unto our feet,
illuminating the pathway that

00:06:12.759 --> 00:06:16.180
will enable us to
truly see one another,

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.680
to respect one another,
to love one another,

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:24.080
and to stand together as
one-- to stand together

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.110
against injustice,
intolerance, and hatred.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.759
Our lights must shine so bright
that others will not only

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:35.169
see our great dome
in Killian Court,

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:37.610
but they will see
our good works,

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:42.290
and they will be inspired to
pick up their torches as well.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.979
And finally, we
must use the power

00:06:44.979 --> 00:06:49.530
of the light that is harnessed
within us to eradicate

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:54.070
the darkness that attempts
to cloak individuals

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:59.449
and systems that perpetuate
racism, oppression,

00:06:59.449 --> 00:07:02.900
and violence against any group.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:08.770
MIT, we have been called
for such a time as this.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:23.030
We are the chosen, for we are
called to make a better world.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:29.400
I will do my part,
will you do yours?

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:36.150
Will you do your part
to make a better world?

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.419
Thank you for being here today.

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:37.919
[AUDIENCE APPLAUSE]

